        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "6fce4cd4-6cfc-3753-a638-ed760bd3ec02",
                "word": "excentriekeling",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9333a082-80fe-47d4-a6fb-af30a55da012",
                        "entry_id": "6fce4cd4-6cfc-3753-a638-ed760bd3ec02",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "excentriekelingen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6fd6d6e-fc28-3cc0-9092-89cd74dec5ec",
                        "entry_id": "6fce4cd4-6cfc-3753-a638-ed760bd3ec02",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iemand die een ongewoon, vreemd, abnormaal of onbehoorlijk gedrag vertoont"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b231dda3-739e-492a-ab0b-8369a985f7dd",
                                "sense_id": "d6fd6d6e-fc28-3cc0-9092-89cd74dec5ec",
                                "text": "Peter Madsen. Tot een paar weken terug had niemand van deze man gehoord. Inmiddels weet heel de wereld wie hij is. Een excentriekeling die zelf een duikboot heeft gebouwd. Een duikboot die recent zonk, waarbij de Zweedse journaliste Kim Wall in eerste instantie spoorloos verdween."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c7ba29a-4d34-4873-ab51-025b4e10d9ed",
                                "sense_id": "d6fd6d6e-fc28-3cc0-9092-89cd74dec5ec",
                                "text": "Het Gemeentemuseum in Den Haag gaat de strijd aan met het eenzijdige beeld dat bij velen is overgebleven van beeldend kunstenaar Anton Heyboer: dat van de excentriekeling met zijn vijf vrouwen, waar de roddelpers met grote regelmaat over schreef. De kunsttempel wil eerherstel voor het werk van Heyboer (1924-2005)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa50f81e-bd19-47ee-9e99-2c2c8855bddb",
                        "source_entry_id": "6fce4cd4-6cfc-3753-a638-ed760bd3ec02",
                        "source_sense_id": "d6fd6d6e-fc28-3cc0-9092-89cd74dec5ec",
                        "target_lang_word": "eccentric character",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a1b77958-26c6-4b41-904e-f87bdecf34c9",
                        "source_entry_id": "6fce4cd4-6cfc-3753-a638-ed760bd3ec02",
                        "source_sense_id": "d6fd6d6e-fc28-3cc0-9092-89cd74dec5ec",
                        "target_lang_word": "eccentric",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eccentric",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d390208-0192-3efd-bfcb-76ea9ddd1ec0",
                                        "entry_id": "1beea2ed-ca38-3ff9-bf91-2a9d6ba09d18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not at or in the centre; away from the centre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "061857a0-08b2-448f-bddc-af77982b8f37",
                                                "sense_id": "8d390208-0192-3efd-bfcb-76ea9ddd1ec0",
                                                "text": "Strikingly, we see that party births tend systematically to be at policy positions that are significantly more eccentric than those of surviving parties, whatever decision rule these parties use."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a6224ea-8946-3562-8716-94ebb377d926",
                                        "entry_id": "1beea2ed-ca38-3ff9-bf91-2a9d6ba09d18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not perfectly circular; elliptical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db95042e-e45f-4a38-98eb-255fa62555a4",
                                                "sense_id": "4a6224ea-8946-3562-8716-94ebb377d926",
                                                "text": "As of 2008, Margaret had the most eccentric orbit of any moon in the solar system, though Nereid's mean eccentricity is greater."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d4f24e6-e938-3722-afb2-2f0c574aa6dd",
                                        "entry_id": "1beea2ed-ca38-3ff9-bf91-2a9d6ba09d18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a different center; not concentric."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4aa021ec-9e4f-3843-97e7-235f236c7d45",
                                        "entry_id": "1beea2ed-ca38-3ff9-bf91-2a9d6ba09d18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deviating from the norm; behaving unexpectedly or differently; unconventional and slightly strange."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae523639-8391-4528-87c6-ff1f89af485b",
                                                "sense_id": "4aa021ec-9e4f-3843-97e7-235f236c7d45",
                                                "text": "1801, Author not named, Fyfield (John), entry in Eccentric Biography; Or, Sketches of Remarkable Characters, Ancient and Modern, page 127,\nHe was a man of a most eccentric turn of mind, and great singularity of conduct."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8033075b-a877-45f1-8eba-69bfce3b543a",
                                                "sense_id": "4aa021ec-9e4f-3843-97e7-235f236c7d45",
                                                "text": "Such is not the case with Mr. Martin Van Butchell, one of the most eccentric characters to be found in the British metropolis, and a gentleman of indisputable science and abilities, but whose strange humors and extraordinary habits, have rather tended to obscure than to display the talents he possessed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4aa6658-7887-4959-89c4-899403bbf499",
                                                "sense_id": "4aa021ec-9e4f-3843-97e7-235f236c7d45",
                                                "text": "There can be no doubt that as a matter of fact a religious life, exclusively pursued, does tend to make the person exceptional and eccentric."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6bc52f7-3fdd-449d-9848-810b8c6487ea",
                                                "sense_id": "4aa021ec-9e4f-3843-97e7-235f236c7d45",
                                                "text": "Khedron was the only other person in the city who could be called eccentric—and even his eccentricity had been planned by the designers of Diaspar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50571508-988d-31bf-982f-6dc753e95522",
                                        "entry_id": "1beea2ed-ca38-3ff9-bf91-2a9d6ba09d18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Against or in the opposite direction of contraction of a muscle (such as results from flexion of the lower arm (bending of the elbow joint) by an external force while contracting the triceps and other elbow extensor muscles to control that movement; opening of the jaw while flexing the masseter)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a motion"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3efb0165-c847-3a01-8108-164ca8c03395",
                                        "entry_id": "1beea2ed-ca38-3ff9-bf91-2a9d6ba09d18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having different goals or motives."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9ae50dc-ed26-461a-ac80-8cd8ce23964e",
                                                "sense_id": "3efb0165-c847-3a01-8108-164ca8c03395",
                                                "text": "a. 1626, Francis Bacon, 1867, Richard Whately (analysis and notes), James R. Boyd (editor), Essay XI: Wisdom for a Man's Self, Lord Bacon's Essays, page 171,\n[…] for whatsoever affairs pass such a man's hands he crooketh them to his own ends, which must needs be often eccentric to those of his master or state: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b19e9c2-7f71-3999-bd0f-c50b0bbd76df",
                                        "entry_id": "1beea2ed-ca38-3ff9-bf91-2a9d6ba09d18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having or being an oospore with a single large oil globule on one side that displaces much of the ooplasm and forces the ooplasts to one side."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e130ea4-e096-4b47-8f01-293775505264",
                                                "sense_id": "1b19e9c2-7f71-3999-bd0f-c50b0bbd76df",
                                                "text": "Oospores may be centric, subcentric, subeccentric or eccentric. Antheridial branches may or may not be present, and are androgynous, monoclinous, diclinous or hypogynous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "eccentric",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3351dfb2-2fa8-39a3-990a-c5fbf9bf7991",
                                        "entry_id": "b838b7d3-b463-3c04-85ae-23f0a26ebf4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who does not behave like others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e72fd97-24b6-42d4-b1a6-408d2cf740b8",
                                                "sense_id": "3351dfb2-2fa8-39a3-990a-c5fbf9bf7991",
                                                "text": "A tiny, feisty woman who always spoke her mind, Charlotte was an eccentric in the wonderful way that some women from the last century were natural eccentrics."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "066cc871-a54b-48b1-9e4f-3d8f97797e81",
                                                "sense_id": "3351dfb2-2fa8-39a3-990a-c5fbf9bf7991",
                                                "text": "Eccentrics live longer, happier, and healthier lives than conformist normal citizens, according to the neuropsychologist David Weeks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f401142-a97c-3992-82dc-256dfd9db940",
                                        "entry_id": "b838b7d3-b463-3c04-85ae-23f0a26ebf4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A kook; a person of bizarre habits or beliefs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b1e1896-04de-34bd-a397-47d652a8d1d5",
                                        "entry_id": "b838b7d3-b463-3c04-85ae-23f0a26ebf4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A circle not having the same centre as another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1fcde927-d5ff-3ee8-a256-84d5ed5d8c36",
                                        "entry_id": "b838b7d3-b463-3c04-85ae-23f0a26ebf4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A disk or wheel with its axis off centre, giving a reciprocating motion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f08dd1b-37e3-4b43-bac5-997276c50a0e",
                                                "sense_id": "1fcde927-d5ff-3ee8-a256-84d5ed5d8c36",
                                                "text": "The position of the eccentrics which is necessary to make the pistons drive the engine forward must be directly the reverse of that which would cause them to drive the engine backwards. To be able, therefore, to reverse the motion of the engine, it would only be necessary to be able to reverse the position of the eccentrics, which may be accomplished by either of two expedients."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e9ab04a-e46e-4dab-856b-c92cb528b64c",
                                                "sense_id": "1fcde927-d5ff-3ee8-a256-84d5ed5d8c36",
                                                "text": "Clavius goes on to use the large number of orbs in Fracostoro's theory as another reason to prefer the Ptolemaic system, then couples this issue with that of the relative capacity of the theories to save the phenomena, then finally reiterates the lack (as he sees it) of conflict between the Aristotelian natural philosophy and the eccentrics and epicycles of mathematical astronomy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "039a8cfe-6969-45c5-87db-2eb452215bc5",
                                                "sense_id": "1fcde927-d5ff-3ee8-a256-84d5ed5d8c36",
                                                "text": "The discussion that revolved around the admissibility of eccentrics and epicycles lied^([sic]) at the core of this theoretical discussion, and those who would not allow such concepts took the position that such eccentrics and epicycles would then introduce a center of heaviness, other than the Earth, around which celestial simple objects would then move."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cadced0b-07a7-3835-923a-2d08f3a4c554",
                                        "entry_id": "b838b7d3-b463-3c04-85ae-23f0a26ebf4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An exercise that goes against or in the opposite direction of contraction of a muscle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "442806ef-321f-4524-a55d-e018a98a13a3",
                                                "sense_id": "cadced0b-07a7-3835-923a-2d08f3a4c554",
                                                "text": "Research tells us that eccentrics, heavy partials, and static exercise may require several days or weeks of recovery time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
